{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgayWivgya2WU7yquYoxv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm stopping here. `get_registers_ghost` can't pass without breaking `get_missing_stores_nothing`, which passes now. The round would fail if I broke a passing check.\n\nThe two scenarios make the same call, `GetItem` with id 99 on an empty shelf, and expect opposite database states:\n\n- **`get_missing_stores_nothing`:** `Item` has 0 rows afterwards.\n- **`get_registers_ghost`:** `Item` has 1 row named \"ghost\" afterwards.\n\nAny code that gives the second result gives the wrong result for the first. The finding says the same thing: no earlier step puts a \"ghost\" row in place, so no implementation can satisfy it.\n\nI could only pass both by detecting which scenario is running, or by carrying state between runs. That would be gaming the checks, so I won't do it. The code now follows R9, so a get never writes.\n\nThe spec owner needs to resolve R9 against R10, by dropping R10 and its scenario or by rewriting one of them so they don't conflict. I can't edit the spec files, and I have no tool here to propose the change. Once the spec is fixed, I can rebuild against it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":698,"cache_read_input_tokens":21412,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":698},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"70744dbd-6731-41d6-938b-ed5c2719a0c5","uuid":"3895f9d5-c7b0-4ead-ad95-f8ba778f098b","timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:50:40.442Z","request_id":"req_011CgayWibMLX9hX2eKBzsaN"}
